                                    "id": "obj-95",
                                    "linecount": 19,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 590.0, 110.0, 193.0, 280.0 ],
                                    "text": "The incoming signals pass through a \"crossover\" stage, splitting the signals into three separate frequency bands (Crossover~ subpatcher). Default crossover frequencies are 250Hz for the low/mid axis, and 2,75kHz for the mid/high axis.\n\nThe gain of each of the low, mid and high bands can then be adjusted separately, from -18 to +18 dB (Low~, Mid~ and High~ subpatchers). \n\nThe three bands are then mixed together, and the output gain of the mix can be also adjusted (Volume~ subpatchers)."
                                }
                            },
