                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "fontface": 0,
                                    "id": "obj-52",
                                    "linecount": 23,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 380.0, 100.0, 227.0, 338.0 ],
                                    "text": "This EQ consists in 7 cascaded filters. \n\nLow and high bands use shelving filters. When using a low or high shelf, all frequencies below or above the chosen frequency are affected by the amount of cut or boost.\n\nThe 5 intermediate filters are peak-notch filters, which only alter frequency bands around specific central frequencies. The bandwidth is specified by a Q or slope factor. In the present case, Q is set to 1. for all filters.\n\nFilters are all biquads. A biquad filter is a two-pole, two-zero second-order filter with a 12dB/octave slope. To facilitate the specification of each filter (type, Q or frequency), we're using the filtercoeff~ object, a signal-rate filter coefficient generator. The controls modulate the gain of each filter."
                                }
                            },
